Method 1: Immediate Stop
Triggers: As soon as validation loss increases even once

Sensitivity: Very sensitive - stops at the first sign of trouble

Use case: When you want to be very conservative and stop at the earliest possible overfitting signal

In your data: Stops at epoch 3 (0.47 > 0.45)

Method 2: Patience
Triggers: Only after validation loss fails to improve for multiple consecutive epochs

Sensitivity: Less sensitive - allows for temporary fluctuations

Use case: When you expect some noise/fluctuation in validation loss and want to give the model a chance to recover

In your data: Stops at epoch 7 (after epochs 6-7 both didn't beat the best loss of 0.42)

