Real-world Analogy:
Method 1: Like stopping a workout as soon as your performance drops once

Method 2: Like stopping a workout only after your performance has been poor for several sets in a row

Method 2 is almost always preferred in practice because validation loss can fluctuate naturally, and you don't want to stop training prematurely due to random noise.






































